<node id="Seoul">
  <data key="d0">Seoul</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Seoul is a city in South Korea that serves as its capital. It is notable for addressing various social and infrastructure issues, including the discussions around loan support where individual low-credit loan options are reportedly missing. The city has been proactive in managing water supply concerns, with authorities implementing measures to tackle water supply issues and offering water fee reduction benefits to its residents. The management of the water supply termination process is also handled by the water supply office in Seoul, indicating a structured approach to addressing water service continuity.

In the context of public health and safety, Seoul has implemented Social Distancing Level 2 measures, particularly aimed at controlling public gatherings, reflecting its commitment to managing health crises. Additionally, Seoul is recognized for its cultural vibrancy, hosting numerous cultural events and providing various facilities that enhance its status as a cultural hub. The city's drinking water, known as Arisu tap water, is supplied and undergoes regular quality testing, which underscores the importance of ensuring safe and reliable water resources for its inhabitants. Overall, Seoul exemplifies a dynamic urban environment that balances social welfare, public health, and cultural enrichment.&lt;SEP&gt;Seoul is the capital city of South Korea, where Guro-gu is located and the Guro G Festival is held.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-798442eb48b371e7be4ca7d3cf14098c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4af5a3553056603378e18742081f811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd3d9738621636ff604645c3110d93d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cda3abda4c6819aedd3f0c6a84c21d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9af6c5ec838421d3638d894a06edce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0928e60540839c3ce03e7a599712cad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6417f794db060808b5c639a8f93ec8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fffd9e71d21770dc7f07084c09890a46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c0d7fe3279d51466ea2db023742542</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
