<node id="Leak">
  <data key="d0">Leak</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Leak represents a potential loss of water, which could lead to increased water bills and requires investigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a9bbf7a94b6250c06b1f762921ca7f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762847549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indoor Leak">
  <data key="d0">Indoor Leak</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An Indoor Leak indicates a water leak within a building that may not be immediately visible and can inflate water bills.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a9bbf7a94b6250c06b1f762921ca7f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762847549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leak Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Leak Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Leak Reduction refers to the procedure by which customers can apply for a reduction in their water bills after identifying and repairing leaks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a9bbf7a94b6250c06b1f762921ca7f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762847549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Waterworks Office">
  <data key="d0">Waterworks Office</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Waterworks Office is the governing body responsible for handling inquiries and requests related to water services and leak detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a9bbf7a94b6250c06b1f762921ca7f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762847549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overcharged Water Bill">
  <data key="d0">Overcharged Water Bill</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An Overcharged Water Bill refers to the bill issued to customers that reflects excessively high charges due to leaks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a9bbf7a94b6250c06b1f762921ca7f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762847549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application for Leak Detection">
  <data key="d0">Application for Leak Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Application for Leak Detection involves formally requesting an inspection by the Waterworks Office to identify possible leaks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a9bbf7a94b6250c06b1f762921ca7f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762847549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application for Bill Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Application for Bill Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Application for Bill Reduction is the formal request submitted to receive a deduction on the water bill after confirming a leak has been repaired.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a9bbf7a94b6250c06b1f762921ca7f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762847549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Usage">
  <data key="d0">Water Usage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Water Usage refers to the quantity of water consumed by a household, which can affect billing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a9bbf7a94b6250c06b1f762921ca7f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762847549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Excessive Charges">
  <data key="d0">Excessive Charges</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Excessive Charges indicate a significant increase in billing due to unexpected factors such as leaks.</data>
