<node id="COVID-19">
  <data key="d0">COVID-19</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">COVID-19 is a global pandemic caused by the infectious disease associated with the novel coronavirus SARS-CoV-2. This virus has led to widespread health concerns, triggering significant disruptions in everyday life, including the closure of childcare facilities and access restrictions to emergency medical services for symptomatic patients.

As a contagious disease, COVID-19's prevention strategies include the use of masks, social distancing measures, and proper hygiene practices. The pandemic prompted various measures aimed at reducing transmission, such as limiting gatherings and promoting physical distancing. Despite its global impact, no direct treatment for COVID-19 has been proven effective, necessitating a reliance on symptomatic care for those affected by the disease. 

Additionally, the pandemic has highlighted the importance of public health interventions and contributed to ongoing discussions regarding prevention and healthcare access during widespread health emergencies.&lt;SEP&gt;COVID-19 is a global pandemic affecting travel protocols, including quarantine and testing requirements for infected travelers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89f8ba55525667ff35cc1fd6f781c500&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd3d9738621636ff604645c3110d93d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cbf32d6c60e826691bf3de959006956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9a9d4881725e6c5709d00d7ff42824b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0928e60540839c3ce03e7a599712cad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fd50c360c8172eddb13644a1ff21589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6417f794db060808b5c639a8f93ec8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bac2bcba467c50a4ab9063db91cbd5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-720010d9735ee34836c2458a4d25df98</data>
